-- title:
--   Ordinary line in the λ-adic eigenplane of J₀(M)
-- statement:
--   Let $M\ge 1$, let $g$ be a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform in the sense of the project (a normalised eigenform whose system of eigenvalues away from the level does not already occur at a proper divisor of $M$), let $\lambda$ be a prime and $S$ a finite set of naturals with $\lambda\in S$ and containing every prime divisor of $M$, and assume $\lambda\nmid M$. Let $O'$ be a characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation domain with finite residue field in which $\lambda$ lies in the maximal ideal, let $\chi_g$ be a ring homomorphism to $\mathbb{C}$ from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 (S \ {lam})`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of the cusp forms generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for $\ell\nmid M$, $\ell\notin S\setminus\{\lambda\}$ and $U_q$ for primes $q\mid M$, $q\notin S\setminus\{\lambda\}$) sending each such $T_\ell$ to the $\ell$-th $q$-coefficient of $g$, and let $\iota$ be a ring homomorphism from the range of $\chi_g$ to $O'$ such that $\iota(\chi_g(T_\lambda))$ is a unit. Let $O''$ be a further characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation domain with finite residue field, finite as an $O'$-algebra with local structure map and a $\mathbb{Z}_\lambda$-algebra, and let $K$ be a fraction field of $O''$. Equip $J_0(M)=\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the level-$M$ modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with its `heckeModuleBar` structure over $\mathrm{HeckeAlg}=\mathbb{Z}[X_\ell:\ell \text{ prime}]$, and let $T=$ [`TateModule lam (JZero M)`](def/EllipticCurve_TateModule.html#L15) be the module of sequences $x:\mathbb{N}\to J_0(M)$ with $x_0=0$ and $\lambda\, x_{n+1}=x_n$. Assume given: a $\mathbb{Z}_\lambda$-module structure on $T$ acting on the $n$-th entry through reduction modulo $\lambda^n$; a homomorphism $\rho_M$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ to $\mathrm{End}_{O''}(O''\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_\lambda}T)$ induced by the Galois action on sequences and adically continuous (for each $n$ some finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ whose pointwise stabiliser moves every vector only inside $\mathfrak{m}^n$ times the module); a ring homomorphism $TM$ from $\mathrm{HeckeAlg}$ to the same endomorphism ring induced by the Hecke action; and a $K$-submodule $W$ of $K\otimes_{O''}(O''\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_\lambda}T)$ of dimension $2$, stable under all base-changed $\rho_M\sigma$, on which the Hecke generator at each prime $\ell\nmid M$ with $\ell\notin S$, and also the generator at $\lambda$, act by the scalar $\iota(\chi_g(T_\ell))$, respectively $\iota(\chi_g(T_\lambda))$, pushed into $K$, and for which the trace on $W$ of any Frobenius at such $\ell$ attached to a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $\ell$ equals that same scalar. Then for every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\lambda$ a non-unit of $A$ there is a $K$-line $L\le W$ stable under the base-changed $\rho_M\sigma$ for all $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, and such that $(\rho_M\sigma)(w)-w\in L$ for every $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and every $w\in W$.
--
--   This is Deligne's ordinarity statement at a prime $\lambda$ of good reduction for the $\lambda$-adic representation attached to a weight-two newform with $a_\lambda$ a unit, formulated at the level of the eigenplane inside the $\lambda$-adic Tate module of $J_0(M)$: inertia at $\lambda$ moves the plane into a decomposition-stable line, so that the representation restricted to a decomposition group at $\lambda$ is ordinary. It feeds the construction of the rank-two Galois representation over $O''$ together with its ordinary line on which Frobenius acts through the unit root of $X^2-a_\lambda X+\lambda$.
